{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1879018,
  "courseSlug": "nodejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "NodeJS - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20345177",
      "title": "Using the MongoDB Client Module",
      "lectureOrder": 537,
      "videoOrder": 476,
      "sourceHash": "76a770b7812df7f2c1b91c124bf2d7aa47028d277c200134ad8de64300cdd0b5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 4.51,
          "en": "So let's make sure we work with MongoDB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.51,
          "end": 7.44,
          "en": "And for that, we set up this client file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.44,
          "end": 8.82,
          "en": "this helpers client file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.82,
          "end": 11.38,
          "en": "with a connect and a getDb function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.38,
          "end": 14.84,
          "en": "We're calling connect whenever our deno server starts up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.84,
          "end": 16.897,
          "en": "and now we wanna call getDb to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.897,
          "end": 21.26,
          "en": "to the connect database whenever we wanna work with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.26,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "And as a side note, the MongoClient from the Mongo library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 27.9,
          "en": "will automatically take care about the connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.9,
          "end": 29.7,
          "en": "it will manage that connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.7,
          "end": 33,
          "en": "It will even set up multiple simultaneous connections",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33,
          "end": 35.57,
          "en": "and use a concept called connection pooling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.57,
          "end": 39.01,
          "en": "to give us the fastest possible way of working with MongoDB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.01,
          "end": 43.22,
          "en": "So all of that is taken care of by this Mongo module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.22,
          "end": 45.06,
          "en": "We just need to call getDb",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.06,
          "end": 47.29,
          "en": "when we now wanna work with the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.29,
          "end": 49.16,
          "en": "And of course there are various places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.16,
          "end": 50.71,
          "en": "where we do wanna work with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "One obvious place is when we want to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 57.03,
          "en": "to our todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.03,
          "end": 60.03,
          "en": "So here in this get todos route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 63.55,
          "en": "I now I want to call getDb to get access to a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.55,
          "end": 65.54,
          "en": "and then call collection on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.54,
          "end": 69.02,
          "en": "to connect to a specific collection in that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.02,
          "end": 71.92,
          "en": "And since we're the one managing the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.92,
          "end": 75.22,
          "en": "we could expect a todos collection, the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.22,
          "end": 77.26,
          "en": "but of course, you should then be consistent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.26,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "when you connect to that collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 83.02,
          "en": "So we assume that there will be a todos collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.02,
          "end": 86.97,
          "en": "If there won't be, it will be created on the fly by MongoDB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.97,
          "end": 89.08,
          "en": "And by calling the find method on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.08,
          "end": 93.68299999999999,
          "en": "we will actually find all elements in that todos collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.88,
          "end": 97.15,
          "en": "Now find will return a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.15,
          "end": 101.32,
          "en": "So I'll add async here, so that we can await this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.32,
          "end": 104.55,
          "en": "And what we'll get back here are our todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.55,
          "end": 106.41,
          "en": "So we'll get back all the documents",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.41,
          "end": 108.13,
          "en": "that can be found in this collection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.13,
          "end": 109.82300000000001,
          "en": "and that will be all our todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.14,
          "end": 115.12,
          "en": "Now those todos will be in a specific MongoDB format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.12,
          "end": 117.84,
          "en": "These will be objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 121.49,
          "en": "but objects that in the end will have an _id field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.49,
          "end": 125.26,
          "en": "which will be added automatically by MongoDB,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.26,
          "end": 130.26,
          "en": "which will be of type ObjectId, a MongoDB specific type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.69,
          "end": 132.97,
          "en": "And then they will have a text field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.97,
          "end": 135.2,
          "en": "which will be some string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.2,
          "end": 139,
          "en": "So that's how the individual documents here will look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "And here we're, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 142.153,
          "en": "getting an array of such documents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 147.13,
          "en": "So to work with those, I want to transform them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.13,
          "end": 152.13,
          "en": "So my transformed todos will be the todos where I call map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.23,
          "end": 155.01,
          "en": "And that will execute a function on every todo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.01,
          "end": 157.47,
          "en": "and then allows us to transform every todo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.47,
          "end": 158.84,
          "en": "into a new object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.84,
          "end": 161.62,
          "en": "So here we then return this new transformed object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.62,
          "end": 165.37,
          "en": "And there, let's say, I just want to have a id field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.37,
          "end": 168.26,
          "en": "so not _id, but just id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.26,
          "end": 171.933,
          "en": "and that should be our todo._id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.35,
          "end": 177.16,
          "en": "but there we can access $oid field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.16,
          "end": 178.39,
          "en": "Now this might look strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.39,
          "end": 180.87,
          "en": "but this will in the end be a property provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.87,
          "end": 182.32,
          "en": "by the Mongo library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.32,
          "end": 185.2,
          "en": "on the documents it fetches from MongoDB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.2,
          "end": 188.28,
          "en": "And that will hold the generated id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.28,
          "end": 191.4,
          "en": "generated by MongoDB as a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.4,
          "end": 196.29,
          "en": "and not as this strange ObjectId object thing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.29,
          "end": 197.84,
          "en": "So that will be the string id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.84,
          "end": 201.23,
          "en": "which I'll then store in a new id property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.23,
          "end": 203.18,
          "en": "In addition, there will be a text property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.18,
          "end": 204.9,
          "en": "and I wanna keep that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.9,
          "end": 208.303,
          "en": "so I'll simply set text equal to todo.text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210.49,
          "end": 212.76,
          "en": "Now here, we also should assign a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.76,
          "end": 215.45,
          "en": "to not have the implicit any type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.45,
          "end": 218.32999999999998,
          "en": "And I'll set the type here to an object type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.32999999999998,
          "end": 220.86,
          "en": "where we'll have an _id field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.86,
          "end": 222.753,
          "en": "which will be of type ObjectId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.69,
          "end": 228.64,
          "en": "That's now something you can import from the Mongo library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.64,
          "end": 233.64,
          "en": "So I'll copy that URL into todos.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.76,
          "end": 236.61,
          "en": "but I'll not import Mongo client or database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.61,
          "end": 239.06,
          "en": "instead, I'll import ObjectId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.06,
          "end": 242,
          "en": "and this will be a type which we now can use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 242,
          "end": 244.21,
          "en": "And we'll have a text field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.21,
          "end": 246.77,
          "en": "which will have a value of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.77,
          "end": 248.39,
          "en": "So that's now the todo type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 248.39,
          "end": 251.82,
          "en": "as we get it back from MongoDB out of our database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 251.82,
          "end": 254.53,
          "en": "Therefore, that's the type I'm setting on this argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.53,
          "end": 256.3,
          "en": "which will be passed into this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.3,
          "end": 258.55,
          "en": "we pass to map automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.55,
          "end": 261.433,
          "en": "for every todo that is fetched from our collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 262.63,
          "end": 264.92,
          "en": "Therefore in the end, we'll have to transform todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.92,
          "end": 267.48,
          "en": "And those are the todos which should be returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 267.48,
          "end": 268.713,
          "en": "to the client now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.71,
          "end": 272.01,
          "en": "So that's a lot of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 272.01,
          "end": 274.76,
          "en": "But with that, we should now be able to fetch todos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.76,
          "end": 276.3,
          "en": "from the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 279.2,
          "en": "Now in order to see whether that really works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 279.2,
          "end": 281.25,
          "en": "let's also work on the post route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 281.25,
          "end": 283.6,
          "en": "And let's make sure that we can add a new todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 284.44,
          "end": 288.40999999999997,
          "en": "For that, here in create we of course create our new todo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 289.39,
          "end": 292.45,
          "en": "but now I want to get access to the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 292.45,
          "end": 297.29,
          "en": "and then here again to the todos collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 297.29,
          "end": 300.14,
          "en": "Of course, here you should use the same collection name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 300.14,
          "end": 302.39,
          "en": "as here when you get todos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 302.39,
          "end": 304.62,
          "en": "otherwise you're adding and fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 304.62,
          "end": 306.63,
          "en": "to and from different collections,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 306.63,
          "end": 309.08,
          "en": "which will not be a good idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 309.08,
          "end": 312.467,
          "en": "And then here, we can call insertOne,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 313.372,
          "end": 315.172,
          "en": "and this will do just what the name implies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 315.172,
          "end": 316.743,
          "en": "it will insert one new todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 318.12,
          "end": 322.35,
          "en": "Now here actually, since MongoDB will generate an id for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 322.35,
          "end": 325.05,
          "en": "we no longer need to generate it on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 325.05,
          "end": 327.01,
          "en": "So I'll comment this out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 327.01,
          "end": 330.01,
          "en": "And I'll just pass in the new todo like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 330.01,
          "end": 330.843,
          "en": "into insertOne.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 331.96,
          "end": 334.90999999999997,
          "en": "Now, of course, since we don't have an id key anymore here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 335.83,
          "end": 338.3,
          "en": "I'll go to my interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 338.3,
          "end": 340.86,
          "en": "And by adding a question mark after id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 340.86,
          "end": 343.07,
          "en": "I actually make this optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 343.07,
          "end": 345.51,
          "en": "so that TypeScript won't complain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 345.51,
          "end": 348.283,
          "en": "if we create a todo object without an id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 349.7,
          "end": 353.06,
          "en": "So with that change made, we can create this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 353.06,
          "end": 355.123,
          "en": "and we can feed it into insertOne.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 358.33,
          "end": 360.86,
          "en": "And now here we can await this action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 360.86,
          "end": 363.71,
          "en": "because insertOne will return a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 363.71,
          "end": 365.3,
          "en": "And this promise will resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 365.3,
          "end": 367.81,
          "en": "whenever the insertion finished.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 367.81,
          "end": 370.3,
          "en": "In that case will then thereafter get information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 370.3,
          "end": 374.78,
          "en": "about the id that was autogenerated by MongoDB",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 374.78,
          "end": 376.28,
          "en": "for the new todo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 376.28,
          "end": 379.743,
          "en": "and they offer now we can manipulate the new todo here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 381.5,
          "end": 384.81,
          "en": "And we can now add the id property on the fly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 384.81,
          "end": 387.73,
          "en": "and set it equal to id, but not like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 387.73,
          "end": 390.49,
          "en": "Instead, id will be of type ObjectId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 390.49,
          "end": 393.26,
          "en": "and therefore again, we'll be able to access $oid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 394.21,
          "end": 396.38,
          "en": "to get this id as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 396.38,
          "end": 398.23,
          "en": "That's simply a specific property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 398.23,
          "end": 400.39300000000003,
          "en": "that exists on the ObjectId type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 401.381,
          "end": 403.2,
          "en": "That will then be our new todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 403.2,
          "end": 405.85,
          "en": "So we'll then have our new todo with the text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 405.85,
          "end": 408.15999999999997,
          "en": "and with the autogenerated id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 408.15999999999997,
          "end": 410.59000000000003,
          "en": "We don't need to add this to our local array anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 410.59000000000003,
          "end": 413.853,
          "en": "we can get rid of that, and we still return it however.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 414.86,
          "end": 416.69,
          "en": "And if we now save all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 416.69,
          "end": 418.87,
          "en": "we can quit that backend server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 418.87,
          "end": 421.96,
          "en": "and rerun it with deno run allow net.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 421.96,
          "end": 424.68,
          "en": "And this will now download the MongoDB package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 424.68,
          "end": 426.9,
          "en": "and try to start our server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 426.9,
          "end": 429.4,
          "en": "But for me, it crashes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 429.4,
          "end": 431.55,
          "en": "Why does this happen?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 431.55,
          "end": 436.55,
          "en": "Well, under the hood, this Mongo module uses a Rust plugin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 437.22,
          "end": 440.06,
          "en": "I mentioned that Deno would be written with Rust,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 440.06,
          "end": 442.09,
          "en": "and that the Mongo module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 442.09,
          "end": 445.55,
          "en": "in the end just wraps the Rust Mongo package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 445.55,
          "end": 448.87,
          "en": "Now this is something which is actively supported by Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 448.87,
          "end": 452.47,
          "en": "But it uses a feature built into Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 452.47,
          "end": 454.90999999999997,
          "en": "which is called plugins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 454.90999999999997,
          "end": 457.65,
          "en": "So under the hood Deno has a plugin system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 457.65,
          "end": 461.18,
          "en": "and the Mongo library uses this system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 461.18,
          "end": 464.4,
          "en": "Now currently, at the point of time I'm recording this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 464.4,
          "end": 465.65999999999997,
          "en": "this is only supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 465.65999999999997,
          "end": 469.42,
          "en": "if we add the unstable flag to our execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 469.42,
          "end": 471.54,
          "en": "This might not be the case in the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 471.54,
          "end": 473.45,
          "en": "but currently it is the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 473.45,
          "end": 475.04,
          "en": "So when we run our app.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 475.04,
          "end": 478.27,
          "en": "we need to add --unstable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 478.27,
          "end": 481.25,
          "en": "Even with that, however, it will still fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 481.25,
          "end": 485.53,
          "en": "It now fails with a PermissionDenied error for reading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 485.53,
          "end": 487.92,
          "en": "Because it turns out that the Mongo library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 487.92,
          "end": 490.21,
          "en": "also wants to read some files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 490.21,
          "end": 494.69,
          "en": "So we should also add --allow-read here as a permission,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 494.69,
          "end": 496.94,
          "en": "and then try executing this again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 496.94,
          "end": 500.09,
          "en": "But now you see, it also wants write access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 500.09,
          "end": 504.02,
          "en": "So let's add this as well, allow-write.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 504.02,
          "end": 508.133,
          "en": "And with that added, now it's downloading the Mongo library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 509.1,
          "end": 511.5,
          "en": "And it crashes with a plugin error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 511.5,
          "end": 514.16,
          "en": "that's the last permission we need to add, promised,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 514.16,
          "end": 515.91,
          "en": "I'm just showing all these errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 515.91,
          "end": 519.14,
          "en": "so that you see that we really need those permissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 519.14,
          "end": 523.64,
          "en": "The last permission we need to add here is --allow-plugin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 523.64,
          "end": 525.68,
          "en": "So you see that this Deno application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 525.68,
          "end": 528.4,
          "en": "now needs a lot of permissions already to run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 528.4,
          "end": 530.64,
          "en": "And that's, by the way, all is what I meant earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 530.64,
          "end": 532.56,
          "en": "We're now granting all those permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 532.56,
          "end": 535.28,
          "en": "and we're again trusting the Mongo library,",
